    "body": "> the output of the `test` string is `1`\r\n\r\nThat means you simply don't have `/usr/local/bin` directory. Zero means the directory is there.\r\n\r\n> installing with the `--bin-dir` flag gives this error `--: line 338: $2: unbound variable`\r\n\r\nThat throws here: https://github.com/starship/starship/blob/ae6c69b13bfc86ba50e3dc11ff927727f55d712f/install/install.sh#L338\r\nThe only way how that could happen is if you add `--bin-dir` without an argument. Double-check that you have put that final dot: `--bin-dir .` ⚠️ ",
